KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only; passes with gcc 11-15
headers.  Reproduce by preprocessing with g++-16 -E (the predefined macros
select the code paths) and running cbmc on the .ii file.
Symptom: "static assertion failed: same reference type" and main dropped.
The cv-differing case common_reference_with<W &, const W &> fails with every
libstdc++ (cpp20_common_reference_with_cv_differing_references).
2026-09-25: PASSES with gcc 16.0.1 headers (g++-16 -E in the gcc16-test
image, cbmc on the .ii): the same-type case was fixed by the round-159/160
work (is_same on reference kinds, compound requirements).  Kept KNOWNBUG
only because this host has no gcc-16 headers to run it under test.pl;
promote to CORE gcc16 on a gcc-16 host.
